    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0360" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00111 Unlawful Shipments/211: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-23T19:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Your No. 26, June 20, 10 a.m. There is no objection to the publication of the
                    documents.</p>
                <pb facs="0361" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/>
                <p>Our records indicate that the planes mentioned as having been found by the
                    insurgents on a Norwegian vessel could not have been shipped from this
                    country.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
